{"name":"Paw Print","hex":"#827a6d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"paw print","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of pawprint."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paw_print"}],"entries":[{"title":"Footprint","blocks":[{"text":"Footprints are the impressions or images left behind by a person walking or running. Hoofprints and pawprints are those left by animals with hooves or paws rather than feet, while \"shoeprints\" is the specific term for prints made by shoes. They may either be indentations in the ground or something placed onto the surface that was stuck to the bottom of the foot. A \"trackway\" is a set of footprints in soft earth left by a life-form; animal tracks are the footprints, hoofprints, or pawprints of an animal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Buzz_Aldrin%27s_bootprint_on_the_Moon%2C_AS11-40-5877.jpg/330px-Buzz_Aldrin%27s_bootprint_on_the_Moon%2C_AS11-40-5877.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Footprint","wikidata":"Q2562511"},{"title":"Paw","blocks":[{"text":"A paw is the soft foot-like part of a mammal, generally a quadruped, that has claws. To paw is for an animal to use their paws, usually gently or for digging, or for a human to use their hands in the manner of an animal's paw."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Paw_and_pads.jpg/330px-Paw_and_pads.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paw","wikidata":"Q219588"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Fu%C3%9Fabdrucke_003_2017_11_15.jpg/500px-Fu%C3%9Fabdrucke_003_2017_11_15.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Fu%C3%9Fabdrucke_003_2017_11_15.jpg/1280px-Fu%C3%9Fabdrucke_003_2017_11